{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "102", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "\"Oh, darling, you look… comfortable,\" Celeste said, adjusting the delicate lace of her emerald green ball gown. Her voice was a melodic chirp.\n\nAcross the living room, Leo shrugged, pulling his sweatshirt further around himself. He had athletic shorts on and worn-out sneakers. \"And you look like you're about to float away. Ready for the Gala?\"\n\nCeleste sighed dramatically. \"Ready as I'll ever be. Honestly, the sheer volume of tulle is a challenge. Are you *sure* you don't want to change? It's the annual charity event, Leo. Important people will be there.\"\n\n\"Important people who are probably just going to talk about investments and who's dating who. I'd rather be comfortable. Besides,\" he gestured to his outfit, \"I'm bringing the snacks. And I know everyone secretly loves my homemade guacamole.\"\n\nCeleste chuckled, a tinkling sound. \"You and your guacamole. Well, alright. Just… try not to spill anything on your… attire. And please, don't mention the guacamole *too* much. I need to maintain a certain level of sophistication.\"\n\nLeo grinned. \"No promises. So, what’s the dress code enforcement like this year? Last year, Mrs. Abernathy nearly had a meltdown because someone wore sandals.\"\n\n\"It's… flexible. Mostly. But I wouldn't want to risk it. *This gown cost more than your entire wardrobe, I suspect.*\" Celeste gave him a pointed look. \"Are you at least going to try to be a little presentable? A nice shirt? Anything?\"\n\n\"Relax, Celeste. I'm presentable. I showered. That's the important thing. *I'll be charming, I promise. And I’ll make sure the champagne flows freely.*\"\n\n\"Very well,\" Celeste conceded, smoothing her skirt. \"Just… try to remember who I am when you're regaling everyone with tales of your guacamole prowess. *And for heaven's sake, don't trip on the red carpet.*\"\n\nLeo laughed. \"Wouldn't dream of it. Now, let’